{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the Python/Go remote surface. Both ports assert",
    "against this file in their own test suites (tests/test_parity.py and",
    "go/internal/parity/parity_test.go), so neither CI job needs the other",
    "toolchain and drift in either port fails that port's build.",
    "",
    "Adding a tool or route means editing this file in the SAME change that adds",
    "it to both ports \u2014 that is the point. The A1 regression (the Python MCP",
    "recall silently missing every ranking knob the Go one had) is exactly the",
    "class of drift this catches.",
    "",
    "CLI commands are deliberately NOT listed: the two CLIs legitimately differ",
    "(Python ships installers as console scripts, Go has `houkai install` and",
    "`houkai config`), so an equality assertion there would be a lie."
  ],
